(877113, 99631, 25553, '<td valign="top">love the pastel colors..they really enhance the romantic look of the pic and the pretty girl up to - 9</td>', 'love the pastel colors..they really enhance the romantic look of the pic and the pretty girl up to - 9', '2004-08-25 15:51:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(877117, 99432, 18197, '<td valign="top">Good idea, but IMO poorly executed. There is a lot in the photo that doesn''t relate to your main idea (book, receipts, drumstick(?), spring, and other background elements). Focus on the fish is a little off, maybe due to glass which you might not be able to help. Composition could be a bit stronger (see threads on rule of thirds). Reflection of the light in the upper right of the bowl distracts. And a bit of work with levels would help, i think. Sorry to seem negative, but if you can go back and reshoot it keeping the above in mind, I think it will seem better to you.</td>', 'Good idea, but IMO poorly executed. There is a lot in the photo that doesn''t relate to your main idea (book, receipts, drumstick(?), spring, and other background elements). Focus on the fish is a little off, maybe due to glass which you might not be able to help. Composition could be a bit stronger (see threads on rule of thirds). Reflection of the light in the upper right of the bowl distracts. And a bit of work with levels would help, i think. Sorry to seem negative, but if you can go back and reshoot it keeping the above in mind, I think it will seem better to you.', '2004-08-25 15:54:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(877120, 99334, 18197, '<td valign="top">Without the title, the tie in to the theme would not be evident. Composition is ok. Lighting, focus, levels and DOF could be improved. As is, the subject seems flat and without emotion. Sorry to be negative, but if these elements could be improved, the photo would "pop" more and feel much more dynamic.</td>', 'Without the title, the tie in to the theme would not be evident. Composition is ok. Lighting, focus, levels and DOF could be improved. As is, the subject seems flat and without emotion. Sorry to be negative, but if these elements could be improved, the photo would "pop" more and feel much more dynamic.', '2004-08-25 15:58:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(877127, 99827, 24970, '<td valign="top">Cropped a little close on top.</td>', 'Cropped a little close on top.', '2004-08-25 16:02:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(877129, 99376, 25979, '<td valign="top">I always enjoy the contrast at a cloud break (especially after a storm).</td>', 'I always enjoy the contrast at a cloud break (especially after a storm).', '2004-08-25 16:03:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(877132, 99060, 25150, '<td valign="top">excellent shot. This says Desperation to me, but kudos to you! 9</td>', 'excellent shot. This says Desperation to me, but kudos to you! 9', '2004-08-25 16:04:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(877133, 99578, 18197, '<td valign="top">Without the title, the tie in to the theme would not be evident.<br/> <br/>There are a few things that would have improved it, I think. The blacks are very black and the whites are very white, and there''s not much in between. If you have photo editing software, try adjusting levels and curves to soften the extreems. This is a basic editing challengs, so selective work with contrast which might have helped the table and drape aren''t allowed, but you might try some selective adjustments to see if they would also help. I can''t really tell where the light is coming from. It feels like there might have been a light from over your left sholder, and possibly one from the right, high up. They are a bit too bright for the fabric, and not quite bright enough for the dog. Possibly a darket fabric would have allowed the lights to work better to smooth out the image.<br/> <br/>I''m sorry if this feels negative, but there are things you can do to make it better. If you can reshoot it with these things in mind, or even re-edit it, you may find you like the results better.</td>', 'Without the title, the tie in to the theme would not be evident. There are a few things that would have improved it, I think. The blacks are very black and the whites are very white, and there''s not much in between. If you have photo editing software, try adjusting levels and curves to soften the extreems. This is a basic editing challengs, so selective work with contrast which might have helped the table and drape aren''t allowed, but you might try some selective adjustments to see if they would also help. I can''t really tell where the light is coming from. It feels like there might have been a light from over your left sholder, and possibly one from the right, high up. They are a bit too bright for the fabric, and not quite bright enough for the dog. Possibly a darket fabric would have allowed the lights to work better to smooth out the image. I''m sorry if this feels negative, but there are things you can do to make it better. If you can reshoot it with these things in mind, or even re-edit it, you may find you like the results better.', '2004-08-25 16:05:06.000000', NULL, 1),
