(885703, 99439, 26087, '<td valign="top">Good picture</td>', 'Good picture', '2004-08-31 17:15:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(885707, 99937, 23956, '<td valign="top">Good color, and the focus on the tip is good, but the centered composition coupled with the very dark area on one side and the very light area on the other is not very effective. Either cropping way in or taking the shot from a bit more to the left or right would really have helped the composition.</td>', 'Good color, and the focus on the tip is good, but the centered composition coupled with the very dark area on one side and the very light area on the other is not very effective. Either cropping way in or taking the shot from a bit more to the left or right would really have helped the composition.', '2004-08-31 17:16:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(885715, 99578, 23956, '<td valign="top">Good shot, but it needs to be much sharper. Some strong lighting might also help to bring out the dog''s face. Also, The title (referring to brown eyes) doesn''t really work with a black and white shot. Perhaps "I hope these dark eyes work"?</td>', 'Good shot, but it needs to be much sharper. Some strong lighting might also help to bring out the dog''s face. Also, The title (referring to brown eyes) doesn''t really work with a black and white shot. Perhaps "I hope these dark eyes work"?', '2004-08-31 17:19:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(885717, 99928, 23956, '<td valign="top">The candle is so bright (blown highlights) that the rest of the image was underexposed, and I really have no idea what I''m looking at here. It looks like one of my old band medals and some watch bands? You might try using a soft fill light to bring up the level of the rest of the image to make it closer to the brightness of the candle, then underexpose the entire thing to get it back down to the darkness that you want it. You could also crop down the top a bit, that grey space isn''t doing anything for the image.</td>', 'The candle is so bright (blown highlights) that the rest of the image was underexposed, and I really have no idea what I''m looking at here. It looks like one of my old band medals and some watch bands? You might try using a soft fill light to bring up the level of the rest of the image to make it closer to the brightness of the candle, then underexpose the entire thing to get it back down to the darkness that you want it. You could also crop down the top a bit, that grey space isn''t doing anything for the image.', '2004-08-31 17:23:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(885718, 99825, 26087, '<td valign="top">Good image</td>', 'Good image', '2004-08-31 17:23:18.000000', NULL, 1),
