(887466, 98713, 18450, '<td valign="top">Interesting and funny take on the challenge. Nice perspective on the photo. <br/> <br/>I''ve found you get a better light on animals early in the am or later in the afternoon.....less reflection off their coats and would have worked on the bone too. Watch the background of the shot........turn round, move the camera up and down..... just so you don''t get something like the line of grass, trees, fence just above the back. A solid grassy background would have really focussed the eye on the subject. <br/> <br/>Just as you go to take the pic.....say their name. If you''re really lucky they look up and you get the eyes in the pic. The great joy and challenge of animal pics is their wonderful unpredictability.<br/> <br/>sue</td>', 'Interesting and funny take on the challenge. Nice perspective on the photo.  I''ve found you get a better light on animals early in the am or later in the afternoon.....less reflection off their coats and would have worked on the bone too. Watch the background of the shot........turn round, move the camera up and down..... just so you don''t get something like the line of grass, trees, fence just above the back. A solid grassy background would have really focussed the eye on the subject.  Just as you go to take the pic.....say their name. If you''re really lucky they look up and you get the eyes in the pic. The great joy and challenge of animal pics is their wonderful unpredictability. sue', '2004-09-01 08:20:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(887480, 98921, 19978, '<td valign="top">What Dan said. This photo is definitely a winner, just not for <b>this</b> challenge. This will immediately take its place in favorites list!</td>', 'What Dan said. This photo is definitely a winner, just not for this challenge. This will immediately take its place in favorites list!', '2004-09-01 08:26:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(887487, 99349, 24413, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone who commented.  I had a vision for this challenge and I''m very pleased with the outcome.  And special thanks to my Mom for being my model and letting me cover her hand in dirt!</td>', 'Thanks to everyone who commented.  I had a vision for this challenge and I''m very pleased with the outcome.  And special thanks to my Mom for being my model and letting me cover her hand in dirt!', '2004-09-01 08:29:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(887494, 99705, 14386, '<td valign="top">Many many thanks.  I am very pleased with my top 5 finish. It was a tedious job deciding on my entry as I have 5 choices. Now, it is irrelevant to ask myself if I could have done better if I submitted another one of my 4 other choices. I am glad it has an above 6 average score.<br/> <br/>Zoomdak, JPR and mrsamsa, I will be very surprised if you can guess my fairy tale entry. BradP, no coaching please. <br/> <br/>Anyway, thank you for the very good comments.<br/> <br/>Manny</td>', 'Many many thanks.  I am very pleased with my top 5 finish. It was a tedious job deciding on my entry as I have 5 choices. Now, it is irrelevant to ask myself if I could have done better if I submitted another one of my 4 other choices. I am glad it has an above 6 average score. Zoomdak, JPR and mrsamsa, I will be very surprised if you can guess my fairy tale entry. BradP, no coaching please.  Anyway, thank you for the very good comments. Manny', '2004-09-01 08:34:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(887498, 98576, 14386, '<td valign="top">Very good Thamer! A moving image with a nice play of light. This should have ribboned. (It is actually more powerful and effective than my 5th placer.)<br/> <br/>Manny</td>', 'Very good Thamer! A moving image with a nice play of light. This should have ribboned. (It is actually more powerful and effective than my 5th placer.) Manny', '2004-09-01 08:43:10.000000', NULL, 0),
