(891406, 99909, 1827, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Rooster:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by svahdat:</b></div><hr/><i> Get a life </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>too bad this guy didnt have anything constructive to say...<br/> <br/>I feared this would not do so well despite fitting the challenge better than most, IMO.<br/>Technically it''s a nice shot... too bad folks can see past there own crap.<br/>Takes guts to do this. Big Ups for it! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I completely agree.  I scored you an 8.  Good job.</td>', 'Originally posted by Rooster: Originally posted by svahdat: Get a life   too bad this guy didnt have anything constructive to say... I feared this would not do so well despite fitting the challenge better than most, IMO.Technically it''s a nice shot... too bad folks can see past there own crap.Takes guts to do this. Big Ups for it!   I completely agree.  I scored you an 8.  Good job.', '2004-09-03 15:52:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(891418, 99775, 1827, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Jinjit:</b></div><hr/><i> Wonderful picture! great lighting, original idea! <br/>Too bad so little knew what it was all about. I think it should''ve been in a much higher place.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>I agree - I gave you an eight.  You deseved to place above MANY of the photos that are higher.</td>', 'Originally posted by Jinjit: Wonderful picture! great lighting, original idea! Too bad so little knew what it was all about. I think it should''ve been in a much higher place. I agree - I gave you an eight.  You deseved to place above MANY of the photos that are higher.', '2004-09-03 15:58:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(891587, 99705, 12573, '<td valign="top">5th place is a great showing, but I''m pretty disappointed that this didn''t ribbon.  It''s one of the better shots I''ve seen on the site and, pardon me for saying, it blows the other entries out of the water for portraying hope in a meaningful, emotional way.  This is an immediate classic that I will go back to for reference many times in the future.</td>', '5th place is a great showing, but I''m pretty disappointed that this didn''t ribbon.  It''s one of the better shots I''ve seen on the site and, pardon me for saying, it blows the other entries out of the water for portraying hope in a meaningful, emotional way.  This is an immediate classic that I will go back to for reference many times in the future.', '2004-09-03 17:14:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(891592, 99243, 25189, '<td valign="top">Here you go.  He wears the headlamp around his neck with his collar, and it shines down beneath his chin.<br/> <br/><a href="//grit.homelinux.net/dpc/dog.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//grit.homelinux.net/dpc/dogt.jpg'', strrpos(''//grit.homelinux.net/dpc/dogt.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//grit.homelinux.net/dpc/dogt.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Here you go.  He wears the headlamp around his neck with his collar, and it shines down beneath his chin. ', '2004-09-03 17:16:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(891881, 99787, 18191, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Hello, Di. I''d first like to say that this photo seems a little bit grainy. It doesn''t seem to be an artistically added grain but a color grain which should not really result from a camera such as the 10D. This might have happened due to a bad JPEG compression which, depending on your photo editing software, can be fixed (PM me if you would like help).<br/> <br/>Otherwise...I find the photo fairly uninteresting. It is underexposed and the reflection adds some interest, but there is a lack of a focal point. There is nothing that stands out as the actualy subject of the image. I read your comment, and I now understand your concept of hope. Unfortunately, I believe that your title led us to believe that the hope was in the trees for they were mirrored, hence Mirrored Hope. Without a focal point, the idea of hope isn''t conveyed obviously so a stronger title may have resulted in a higher score.<br/> <br/>As far as this goes for you, I think it is a try again next time situation. Good luck.<br/> <br/>If you have any questions, comments, or concerns feel free to PM me.<br/> <br/>Lee</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Hello, Di. I''d first like to say that this photo seems a little bit grainy. It doesn''t seem to be an artistically added grain but a color grain which should not really result from a camera such as the 10D. This might have happened due to a bad JPEG compression which, depending on your photo editing software, can be fixed (PM me if you would like help). Otherwise...I find the photo fairly uninteresting. It is underexposed and the reflection adds some interest, but there is a lack of a focal point. There is nothing that stands out as the actualy subject of the image. I read your comment, and I now understand your concept of hope. Unfortunately, I believe that your title led us to believe that the hope was in the trees for they were mirrored, hence Mirrored Hope. Without a focal point, the idea of hope isn''t conveyed obviously so a stronger title may have resulted in a higher score. As far as this goes for you, I think it is a try again next time situation. Good luck. If you have any questions, comments, or concerns feel free to PM me. Lee', '2004-09-03 19:56:25.000000', NULL, 0),
