(896118, 99058, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi MotoCycleBoi...<br/> <br/>This is a nice shot for a wedding album.  I can''t really offer you much ''critique'' on a shot of this nature, because you are not in control of the total environment.  There are some elements of this photo that could be better obviously, but without total control, they would not be possible.  One of the most difficult issues of shooting outside is keeping the model''s eyes from sqinting.  It doesn''t look like you were working in sunlight, which is good, but maybe the light behind you is bright enough to make the people squint their eyes.  The wind could also be contributing to that as well...<br/> <br/>Weddings would be fun to shoot.. keep up the good work :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi MotoCycleBoi... This is a nice shot for a wedding album.  I can''t really offer you much ''critique'' on a shot of this nature, because you are not in control of the total environment.  There are some elements of this photo that could be better obviously, but without total control, they would not be possible.  One of the most difficult issues of shooting outside is keeping the model''s eyes from sqinting.  It doesn''t look like you were working in sunlight, which is good, but maybe the light behind you is bright enough to make the people squint their eyes.  The wind could also be contributing to that as well... Weddings would be fun to shoot.. keep up the good work :) John Setzler', '2004-09-06 18:08:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(896124, 99931, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Ancientimages...<br/> <br/>Hummingbirds are interesting creatures.  They have a lot of beauty simply in their petite size and precision motion around my feeders.  <br/> <br/>This photo feels like a bit of a ''wedge'' into this challenge.  When a viewer looks at this photo and tries to evaluate the tie in to the theme of hope, I believe they will be left wanting.  The photo also feels quite underexposed.  The composition here has a bit too much negative space to really make the hummingbird a strong subject.  The blurred background helps, but I believe the bird needs to fill more of the frame here to be successful as a great bird photo.  Its difficult to get close to these guys :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Ancientimages... Hummingbirds are interesting creatures.  They have a lot of beauty simply in their petite size and precision motion around my feeders.   This photo feels like a bit of a ''wedge'' into this challenge.  When a viewer looks at this photo and tries to evaluate the tie in to the theme of hope, I believe they will be left wanting.  The photo also feels quite underexposed.  The composition here has a bit too much negative space to really make the hummingbird a strong subject.  The blurred background helps, but I believe the bird needs to fill more of the frame here to be successful as a great bird photo.  Its difficult to get close to these guys :) John Setzler', '2004-09-06 18:13:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(896137, 99705, 7743, '<td valign="top">*** Critique Club ***<br/> <br/>My first impression is of a well thought out composition.  Even though the girl is looking out of the frame it works here.   <br/> <br/>Even though the background is blown out it is not distracting.  The background being out of focus helps here (DOF is bang on).  The main subject is very sharp and the skintone appears acurate.  A reflector may have helped with the darker areas on the right side of your model.<br/> <br/>Well done.<br/> <br/>Colette</td>', '*** Critique Club *** My first impression is of a well thought out composition.  Even though the girl is looking out of the frame it works here.    Even though the background is blown out it is not distracting.  The background being out of focus helps here (DOF is bang on).  The main subject is very sharp and the skintone appears acurate.  A reflector may have helped with the darker areas on the right side of your model. Well done. Colette', '2004-09-06 18:22:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(896151, 99243, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Krazy...<br/> <br/>This is a neat technique photo, but I believe it is a bit of a stretch on the challenge theme.  The image itself doesn''t seem to relay much on the theme without the title.  The idea here and the effect of light created by your technique is excellent though :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Krazy... This is a neat technique photo, but I believe it is a bit of a stretch on the challenge theme.  The image itself doesn''t seem to relay much on the theme without the title.  The idea here and the effect of light created by your technique is excellent though :) John Setzler', '2004-09-06 18:32:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(896397, 99071, 19035, '<td valign="top">A 6.2+ is a good score, you should be proud - I scored you a 7, looking again, I probably should have gave an 8, sorry.  I love the innosence in your childs eyes, nice shot.</td>', 'A 6.2+ is a good score, you should be proud - I scored you a 7, looking again, I probably should have gave an 8, sorry.  I love the innosence in your childs eyes, nice shot.', '2004-09-06 21:31:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(896417, 99071, 10084, '<td valign="top">This is truly a magnificient scene and tender moment. A slightly closer crop would give a more intimate feeling to the composition. Cropping the left side of your shot closer toward your eyes and cropping up to the right side up your sons shoulder would help to give this feeling.<br/> <br/>The catchlight on your sons'' eyes really make this a beautiful shot and helps the viewers eye look right at it. Your lighting technique on this shot is extremely well done. The contrast on both side of his face make this shots very interesting and appealing.</td>', 'This is truly a magnificient scene and tender moment. A slightly closer crop would give a more intimate feeling to the composition. Cropping the left side of your shot closer toward your eyes and cropping up to the right side up your sons shoulder would help to give this feeling. The catchlight on your sons'' eyes really make this a beautiful shot and helps the viewers eye look right at it. Your lighting technique on this shot is extremely well done. The contrast on both side of his face make this shots very interesting and appealing.', '2004-09-06 21:51:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(896526, 99071, 6520, '<td valign="top">The eyes are fantastic!</td>', 'The eyes are fantastic!', '2004-09-06 22:43:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(896545, 99090, 24976, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by luv2photo:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Louison:</b></div><hr/><i> Hmmm... a convert? Muslim woman with a Christian rosary? Still effective and very well presented. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I wondered the same thing.... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I was trying to create a juxtaposition between the two different cultures while at the same time showing that just maybe co-existance is possible.</td>', 'Originally posted by luv2photo: Originally posted by Louison: Hmmm... a convert? Muslim woman with a Christian rosary? Still effective and very well presented.   I wondered the same thing....   I was trying to create a juxtaposition between the two different cultures while at the same time showing that just maybe co-existance is possible.', '2004-09-06 22:59:16.000000', NULL, 0),
