(902302, 99416, 4871, '<td valign="top">I love this picture! She is absolutely beautiful and I love how the wind is blowing her hair across her face - sublime! My only comment / suggestion would be that on the flowers next to her there are dead flowers - or flowers with no petals at least. It would have definitely added more color to your photograph. Other than that you would have got a 10 from me!</td>', 'I love this picture! She is absolutely beautiful and I love how the wind is blowing her hair across her face - sublime! My only comment / suggestion would be that on the flowers next to her there are dead flowers - or flowers with no petals at least. It would have definitely added more color to your photograph. Other than that you would have got a 10 from me!', '2004-09-09 19:42:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(904771, 99192, 17126, '<td valign="top">I don''t knowanything that would cause someone to score this lower than a 10, but 1''s and 2''s? Even 3''s... way too many. This should have ribboned.<br/> <br/>This is one of the coolest pictures I''ve seen on this site.</td>', 'I don''t knowanything that would cause someone to score this lower than a 10, but 1''s and 2''s? Even 3''s... way too many. This should have ribboned. This is one of the coolest pictures I''ve seen on this site.', '2004-09-11 14:16:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(905893, 98988, 11800, '<td valign="top">If anyone has vision, I think it''s you. But even with that, and pardon me for suggesting it, but the white walls are what I feel let this excellent picture down. Perhaps a darker background with the light shinning up like it is now would have helped isolate Pandora in her own world? Say a blue? Anyway, good idea.</td>', 'If anyone has vision, I think it''s you. But even with that, and pardon me for suggesting it, but the white walls are what I feel let this excellent picture down. Perhaps a darker background with the light shinning up like it is now would have helped isolate Pandora in her own world? Say a blue? Anyway, good idea.', '2004-09-12 15:15:01.000000', NULL, 0),
